From fb9104b205e66adaeb7d438765c07de86cef87c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:56:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Deskbar: an icon for each of the Applications menu's folders

The nine folders the Applications menu is sorted into (patch 0053) all
looked alike. Each now has its own icon: the folder the Deskbar draws
its menus with (Folder_virtual) with an emblem where Haiku's special
folders carry theirs. Accessories a pocket knife (App_ArmyKnife),
Development the bug (Overlay_development), Files Tracker's copying
papers (Tracker_copy), Games a joystick (Prefs_Joystick), Graphics a
palette (App_ImageEditor), Internet the globe (Misc_Earth), Multimedia
two notes (drawn for it), Office a page (Overlay_document), System a
gear (Overlay_gear). The Deskbar draws its menus at 16 pixels, where an
emblem of the usual size is a few specks, so up to 21 pixels (where
Folder_virtual switches to its thicker outline) a larger copy of it is
drawn instead.

- src/data/directory_attrs/deskbar-applications-<folder>.rdef: the
  icons, as the folders' BEOS:ICON attribute. They are made from
  data/artwork/icons by HaikuArmQemu's tools/artwork/deskbar/build.py
  (with hviftool.py, an HVIF <-> SVG converter).
- build/jam/packages/Haiku gives them to the folders of the haiku
  package; packagefs shows a system package's directory attributes
  over other packages'. The ports' packages get the same icon on the
  folders prosepkg makes in them (Games has no Haiku application).
- Tracker: a virtual directory -- every folder of the Deskbar menu is
  one -- is drawn from its definition file, which only had the virtual
  directory type, so a directory's own icon never showed there.
  VirtualDirectoryManager now copies the icon attributes (BEOS:ICON and
  the old bitmap ones) of the first merged directory that has them onto
  the definition file it makes for a subdirectory.

